course: dictionary
lesson: 1992
title: Compulsory: when you have no choice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Compulsory means something must be done because a rule or law says so. You have no choice. «In Australia voting is compulsory for adult citizens» means every adult citizen has to vote, not just the ones who want to.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Shin pads are compulsory, studs-up tackles are fouls» tells you that the rules of the game are strict. Shin pads are a rule you must follow. Ask yourself: would "must" fit here? If it would, compulsory means the same as must.
explain: The opposite of compulsory is optional or voluntary, which means it is your choice. «In the USA, voting is a free choice» shows this. Check your meaning by swapping in "must" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Compulsory means something must be done because a rule or law says so.
fact: The opposite of compulsory is optional or voluntary.
fact: Phrases to know: a compulsory subject, compulsory education, it is compulsory to wear a helmet.
fact: «In Australia, voting in national elections is compulsory for adult citizens»; if you do not vote without a good reason, you may get a small fine.
fact: A seat belt is compulsory by law in cars, so you must wear one every time you travel.
exercise: «Seat belts are compulsory in cars.» What does compulsory mean here? | You can wear one if you feel like it | You only wear one at night | *You must wear one because a law says so | You can take it off whenever you like
exercise: Which word is the opposite of compulsory? | Required | Important | *Optional | Heavy
exercise: Nadia says compulsory is just another word for important. Why is that not quite right? | Compulsory is a colour | Compulsory means something you enjoy doing | Important and compulsory mean exactly the same | *Compulsory means you have to do it because a rule or law says so
test: «In Australia, voting in national elections is compulsory for adult citizens.» Who must vote? | *Adult citizens | Nobody, because it is a free choice | Only people who like politics | Children and visitors
test: Which phrase means a subject that every pupil must study? | Short lesson | *Compulsory subject | Optional subject | Free time
exam: Which sentence shows that something is NOT compulsory, so you have a free choice? | Studs-up tackles are fouls | Seat belts are compulsory by law | *In the USA, voting is a free choice | Shin pads are compulsory
